From 16e03797b8c73d699e97d2df4f1c17cc2a31e241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:52:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): lanes review findings: gate holds against
 decompose/specify, agent identity, rule precedence [daveey]

- gate-held cards are refused by decompose and specify (the auto-decomposer released them after 120 s)
- the user exemption needs a human shell: a worker's CLI create is an agent whatever --created-by says;
  the dashboard counts as the user
- a match rule wins over a tenant an agent passed (workers pass HERMES_TENANT on every create)
- self-work intake matches on the tenant creation will store
- held = triage + gate mark + never ran; exclusions apply only while the gate is enforced
- link release needs a runnable waiter and respects never_admit; kernel recovery cards are not held
- planner: a refused link is one refusal, lane names cannot collide with state, no relane out of a gated lane
- lanes set writes the installation-root config; a manual admit is outside the budget
- an unreadable config never stops creation

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
